* Developed with AI assistance from Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) -- 17 Nov 2026
* rexx.pfx -- REXX definition for the prefix-macro framework (phase B)
* Format: one tag per line, "§tag value" (the marker §, U+00A7, occurs
* in none of the languages, so a value may hold any text such as
* ":ROW." or "::class"); a line starting with * is a
* comment. Rows belong to the §cmd above them; variants select a
* different first row by the command's operand.
*
* Indentation units are named; the macro calls them Indent_<unit> and,
* under CMS, takes overrides from GLOBALV SELECT <macro>.
§lang       REXX
§macro      PFXREXX
*
* Keyword case: the templates as written (ASIS); the user may ask for
* LOWER or UPPER (option <macro>_CASE / GLOBALV PFX_CASE).
§case       asis
§unit       DO=3 IF=3 label=3 SELECT=1 WHEN=2
*
* Mask for the body lines the macro adds (his original): column:text,
* "op" is the statement column of the body line.  Since 18 Nov 2026 (his
* decision) the placeholder there is &placeholder, not ".": a lone "." is
* a valid REXX clause, and overtyping one character needs INSERT.
§mask       40:/* 70:*/ op:&placeholder
*
* Look-back: which lines don't govern indentation.
§comment    /* */
§continue   trailing ,
§blank      skip
§label      colon label
*
* Indentation after the governing line's keyword, and before a command.
§opens      DO=DO ELSE=IF IF=IF SELECT=SELECT WHEN=WHEN OTHERWISE=WHEN
§nested     WHEN OTHERWISE
§dedent     WHEN=WHEN
*
* After a line starting with END (at the body's column), the insert
* aligns with the line the END closes (his original intent).
§closes     END
*
* ---- commands ----
§cmd        DO          §min 2  §desc Insert DO block
§var        -           §first do                        §cursor body
§var        FOREVER 1   §first do forever                §cursor body
§var        UNTIL 1     §first do until &placeholder     §cursor 9
§var        WHILE 1     §first do while &placeholder     §cursor 9
§var        *           §first do %op                    §cursor 3
§row        pend=RIC indent=DO
§row        indent=DO text=end
*
§cmd        IF          §min 2  §desc Insert IF
§first      if &placeholder then do                       §cursor 3
§row        pend=RIC indent=IF
§row        indent=IF text=end
§row        text=else do
§row        pend=RIC indent=IF
§row        indent=IF text=end
*
§cmd        SELECT      §min 3  §desc Insert SELECT block
§first      select
§row        indent=SELECT text=when &placeholder then do  §cursor 5
§row        pend=RIC indent=SELECT+WHEN
§row        indent=SELECT+WHEN text=end
§row        indent=SELECT text=otherwise do
§row        pend=RIC indent=SELECT+WHEN
§row        indent=SELECT+WHEN text=end
§row        indent=SELECT text=end
*
§cmd        WHEN        §min 3  §desc Insert WHEN clause
§first      when &placeholder then do                     §cursor 5
§row        pend=RIC indent=WHEN
§row        indent=WHEN text=end
*
§cmd        OTHERWISE   §min 4  §desc Insert OTHERWISE clause
§first      otherwise do                                  §cursor body
§row        pend=RIC indent=WHEN
§row        indent=WHEN text=end
*
§cmd        ITERATE     §min 4  §desc Insert ITERATE; the cursor follows the keyword, for an optional loop name
§first      iterate                                       §cursor 8
*
§cmd        LEAVE       §min 3  §desc Insert LEAVE; the cursor follows the keyword, for an optional loop name
§first      leave                                         §cursor 6
*
* Engine built-ins this language uses (no template): pending and case
* commands. Synonyms are the names the setup registers.
§builtin    .. CLINE RI RIC CLC CUC
§synonym    LOC=CLC UPC=CUC
